BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ROBERT MOOR & WENDY JACOBS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T200000
UID:260410-uNQ8lfrjUSKd3fXGZv4rA
DESCRIPTION:PETALUMA --\n\nCopperfield's Books and ReLeaf Petaluma are hon
 ored to welcome bestselling and acclaimed author Robert Moor to Petaluma i
 n celebration of his wondrous new book - *In Trees: An Exploration*!\n\nH
 e will be joined in conversation by Wendy Jacobs\, Chair of the ReLeaf A
 dvisory Board and Master Naturalist with over 15 years of urban forestry e
 xperience and social justice leadership.\n\nExtend Earth Day’s reflectio
 n with a rich exploration of the natural world and its layered past\, unco
 vering the lessons trees offer about growth and insight.\n\nAs part of ReL
 eaf’s reforestation efforts\, 10–15 audience members will be invited t
 o take home a locally grown seedling lovingly raised by ReLeaf themselves!
  Recipients will also have the opportunity to participate in ReLeaf’s on
 going stewardship program\, receiving seasonal guidance and light-touch s
 upport to help their trees thrive for years to come.\n\nJoin us for a read
 ing and warm discussion followed by an audience Q&A and book signing with 
 photo opportunities.\n\nThis is a free event\, *registration recommended 
 for seating*.\n\n**From the acclaimed author of the *New York Times* bes
 tseller *On Trails* comes a wondrous new journey through the wilds of nat
 ure and the gnarls of history\, exploring how trees**—**from the mightie
 st sequoia to the tiniest bonsai**—**can teach us to grow wise.**\n\n**
 “With adventurous journeys\, lively storytelling\, and provocative refle
 ction\, Moor invites us to know charismatic forests through the eyes of ot
 her worldviews in order to guide us through these urgent times.” —Rob
 in Wall Kimmerer\, #1 *New York Times*bestselling author of *The Service
 berry***\n\n**“*In Trees* is dazzlingly erudite\, playful\, profound\, 
 adventurous and\, above all\, eloquently\, fiercely *alive*. Full of bril
 liant\, mind-bending insights and wonderful surprises\, this is the most l
 ife-affirming book I’ve read in a long time.”** **—John Vaillant\, 
 National Book Award finalist for *Fire Weather***\n\n*To truly grasp the 
 wisdom of a tree\, you need to begin thinking like one…*\n\nOne day\, on
  a whim\, Robert Moor set out to climb a tree near his home—unwittingly 
 embarking on what would become a decade-long\, globe-spanning adventure of
  intellectual and spiritual transformation. Pursuing the hidden wisdom of 
 trees\, he scales to the very top of a giant sequoia while filming a natur
 e documentary with David Attenborough\; he treks through swamps in Papua t
 o reach a treehouse-dwelling tribe of hunter-gatherers\; and he journeys t
 o a remote research camp in Tanzania\, where he spends a memorable night s
 leeping in a chimpanzee nest\, seeking to understand our deep evolutionary
  history. Eventually\, having gained a radical new outlook on both our gna
 rled past and our ever-branching future\, he joins an intrepid clan of cli
 mate activists risking everything to halt construction of a new oil pipeli
 ne and save an ancient forest.\n\nAlong the way\, Moor learns the art of 
 “tree-thinking\,” which\, he discovers\, has the power to break open s
 ome of humanity’s oldest questions: What is the secret to truly *growin
 g*old? How do we set down deeper roots in an increasingly chaotic world? M
 ost importantly\, how should we—as individuals\, as communities\, as ste
 wards of the earth—live?\n\nA witty and relentlessly curious excursion t
 hrough philosophy\, history\, and science\, what begins as an ode to the m
 iracle of trees blossoms into a joyous\, daring\, fiercely hopeful endeavo
 r to arborize humanity.\n\n**Author: Robert Moor** is the bestselling aut
 hor of *On Trails* and *In Trees*. Translated into more than a dozen lan
 guages\, *On Trails* garnered the National Outdoor Book Award\, the Paci
 fic Northwest Book Award\, and the William Saroyan International Prize. Hi
 s writing has appeared in *The New Yorker* (link)\, *The Atlantic* (link
 )\, *Outside* (link)\, *Harper’s*\, *New York* magazine\, *Emergenc
 e*\, and *n+1*\, among other publications. He lives in Halfmoon Bay\, Brit
 ish Columbia. Visit him at: https://www.robertmoor.com/ and on social: B
 luesky: https://bsky.app/profile/robertmoor.com\n\n**Wendy Jacobs:** Chai
 r of ReLeaf Petaluma and Master Naturalist with over 15 years of urban for
 estry volunteer experience.\n\n**Praise:**\n\n“Robert Moor’s brilliant
  *In Trees* is––like its subject––powerfully\, fascinatingly arb
 orescent. Moving from sky to earth\, Moor unfurls in fine-grained prose th
 e ancient\, urgent story of how trees transform us. Reading it\, I felt my
  senses of time\, life\, and process shift in ways I hadn’t experienced 
 before.” **—Robert Macfarlane\, *New York Times* bestselling author
  of *Is a River Alive?***\n\n“Daring\, inspired\, and wide-ranging\, th
 is is much more than a book about trees. To read this book is to feel ones
 elf anchored more firmly to the earth and\, simultaneously\, to become mor
 e open to life’s many branching\, wild possibilities.” **—Ferris Ja
 br\, *New York Times* bestselling author of *Becoming Earth***\n\n“A 
 profound and loving\, shrewd and funny pilgrimage. Moor finds so much beau
 ty in this bold\, wild search to understand how he should live.” **—L
 arissa MacFarquhar\,** **award-winning** **author of *Strangers Drownin
 g***\n\n“A new book in that rare category of ‘classic upon publication
 .’”**—Bill McKibben\, *New York Times* bestselling author of *Her
 e Comes the Sun***\n\n"Brilliantly written\, supremely intelligent\, and p
 hilosophically provocative." **—*Kirkus Reviews*\, starred review**\n\n
 "Robert Moor is an erudite and delightfully meandering writer (see his On 
 Trails for what I mean) who invariably chooses the more interesting of two
  possible narrative paths... From giant sequoias to the tree-houses of Pap
 uan tribesmen to an actual chimpanzee nest\, Moor makes his way to the top
 s of trees everywhere\, the better to find some perspective."**— Jonny D
 iamond\, Literary Hub**\n\n"Robert Moor is one of the few I'd trust to bri
 ng a fresh perspective to trees and he does not disappoint. By turns earth
 y and philosophical\, what a captivating and exhilarating book!"**—Trist
 an Gooley\, Sunday Times bestselling author of How To Read A Tree**
LOCATION:Copperfield's Books- Petaluma
URL:https://MOOR_TREES_PETALUMA.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
