DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T200000
UID:260415-T58gRm4G0-b-3UJRgvDKQ
DESCRIPTION:Gary Owen has been entertaining audiences for more than two de
 cades with his sharp observational humor and fearless storytelling. Known 
 for his unapologetic\, rule-defying style\, his material draws from his pe
 rsonal life\, time in the military\, and the everyday absurdities that con
 nect people across backgrounds. With a fanbase that has grown by the milli
 ons in recent months and continues to surge across social media\, Owen’s
  reach has cemented his place as one of the most in-demand touring comedia
 ns today.\n\nBeyond stand-up\, Owen has appeared in a wide range of featur
 e films and television. He continues to write\, produce\, and perform his 
 own groundbreaking comedy specials. In addition to his on-stage and on-scr
 een work\, Owen hosts his own podcast\, \\#GetSome with Gary Owen.\n\nAges
  12\\+ Recommended\n\nVIP 1: Gary Owen VIP Meet & Greet Package\n\nPremium
  Seat Ticket\n\nMeet & Greet with Gary Owen\n\nPhoto with Gary Owen\n\nCom
 memorative VIP Laminate\n\nExclusive Autographed Merchandise Item\n\nVIP 2
 : Gary Owen VIP Merchandise Package\n\nPremium Seat Ticket\n\nExclusive Au
 tographed Merchandise Item\n\n\\*No artist participation
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/gary-owen-26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olive Oil Challah Demo at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T120000
UID:260414VSDXqTLC9k2CW8FfC2LFZA
DESCRIPTION:Learn to mix\, knead\, braid\, and bake olive oil challah. Ste
 phanie Rosenbaum Klassen will demonstrate her version of this rich\, soft 
 egg bread made with our estate-grown olive oil and local honey—perfect f
 or any celebration. We’ll also include a recipe (and taste) of Challah F
 rench Toast with Apple Cider Syrup.\n\nThe experience begins with a leisur
 ely walk through our orchard to the Apple Cottage\, where the demo takes p
 lace surrounded by the beauty of the farm. Afterward\, guests will ride ba
 ck to the Farm Shop aboard our beloved apple-themed trolley.\n\nStephanie 
 Rosenbaum Klassen is Gold Ridge Organic Farms' Farm Shop lead\, bringing y
 ears of experience as a cookbook author\, teacher\, and food writer. Her a
 cclaimed books include A Little Taste of San Francisco\, World of Doughnut
 s\, and Honey from Flower to Table. Her work has appeared in The New York 
 Times\, San Francisco Chronicle\, Edible publications\, and more.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600726/oliv
 e-oil-challah-demo-with-stephanie-rosenbaum-klassen
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Trashion" Print Lab: Tetra Pak & Milk Carton Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T193000
UID:260412WHQGcPmLV0-wjbNHQN5bng
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFriday\, April 24\, 2026 5:30 PM – 7:30 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: 
 Printmaking\, Sustainability\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n16\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\
 n\n$15\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$15\n\
 nIn honor of “Trashion Fashion” we are focusing on creative reuse\, an
 d sustainable printmaking! \n\nAbout the Class\n\nRoll up your sleeves an
 d join us for a special evening of “Trashion” Print Lab! Our mission i
 s to explore a creative arts technique socially with our community. Print 
 Lab is not a traditional class\, but an affordable art-making experience. 
 We welcome you to print\, play and experiment with an activity to create s
 omething unique in our printmaking studio!  In honor of “Trashion Fashi
 on” we are focusing on creative reuse\, and sustainable printmaking!  T
 etra Pak printmaking is an eco-friendly and accessible art technique that 
 repurposes used food and beverage cartons – like those for milk\, juice\
 , or broth\, as printing plates. It is a form of intaglio printmaking \\(s
 imilar to drypoint etching\\)\, where you scratch or “incise” a design
  into the carton’s inner foil or plastic lining to create a printable su
 rface. Carton printing is widely considered a highly sustainable alternati
 ve to traditional etching because it prioritizes creative reuse and non-to
 xic processes. Recycle\, repurpose and recreate! Learn how to turn garbage
  into beautiful prints! We will demonstrate how to draw\, scratch\, cut\, 
 ink and print carton surfaces on our presses with water-soluble etching in
 ks. Guests will leave with their own prints they create! We have plenty of
  cartons to share\, but we encourage guests to bring their own cleaned Tet
 ra Pak’s and milk cartons to use or donate to the printmaking studio. No
  printmaking experience is necessary. Light refreshments will be provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/trashion-print-lab-tetra-pa
 k-milk-carton-printing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
