DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T190000
UID:260331XblNLsUkPUe3QyWQea7LXw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special Saturday acoustic live music set at Adob
 e Road Winery in **Downtown Petaluma**. Sip on award-winning wines while 
 enjoying talented local musicians in a warm and inviting atmosphere. Choos
 e from wines by the glass or bottle to discover new favorites. Reserve you
 r spot on **Tock** and make it a memorable night of great music\, fine w
 ine\, and good company!\n\nBorn and raised in San Francisco\, Mike Z joine
 d his first “working” band in high school. Although he started as a tr
 umpet player (which he gave up because he couldn’t talk\, let alone sing
 \, while playing)\, he switched to bass\, and then guitar. Playing in Bay 
 Area bands early in his career\, he had the opportunity to back such acts 
 as The Whispers\, The Pointer Sisters\, and Johnny Taylor.\n\nMike Z has w
 ritten original tunes for film and TV libraries\, and performed on numerou
 s studio tracks.\n\nMike Z appears currently in the bands Z and The Bender
 s and the Mike Z Jazz Trio.
LOCATION:Adobe Road Winery
URL:https://adoberoadwines.com/events/live-music-mike-z-april-25-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We The Sculptors…International Sculpture Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T160000
UID:260331PAAU6ISEGEeA73sLMM9FZg
DESCRIPTION:From ancient monuments carved in stone to bold contemporary ab
 straction\, sculpture has always been a defiant presence in the world. It 
 occupies space and refuses to be ignored.\n\nThis year’s International S
 culpture Days event embraces the belief that sculpture can inspire\, provo
 ke\, and challenge the world around us. Ten Artists will present their wor
 k \, and visitors can engage in acts of “defiant dissidence\,” explori
 ng how art can serve as both personal reflection and public voice.\n\nThe 
 event draws on a long tradition of artists and citizens using visual langu
 age to express dissent\, question norms\, and imagine new possibilities. A
 t its core\, We The Sculptors affirms the enduring role of artists to chal
 lenge\, to question\, and to stand visibly in the public square.
LOCATION:T Barny Gallery & Sculpture Garden
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/we-the-sculptors-intern
 ational-sculpture-days/18433856/2026-04-25T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
