BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wildflower Walk at The Sea Ranch Lodge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T113000
UID:260420zdhUplHEqUayNRdnknZx8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided Wildflower Walk with Katrina along the sc
 enic coastal bluffs at The Sea Ranch Lodge. This relaxed stroll will explo
 re the seasonal wildflowers that bloom along our dramatic shoreline\, with
  time to take in ocean views\, learn about local plants\, and enjoy the be
 auty of the Sonoma Coast. \n\nThis event is complimentary\, but we ask th
 at you please RSVP. Day-of guests are always welcome to join. We will star
 t promptly at 10am.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild Edibles & Coastal Plant Walk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T120000
UID:260420wgDAEFlpDk6u7h6Vf-I9xA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided foraging experience exploring the seasona
 l abundance of our coastal landscape. Learn to identify and harvest wild p
 lants like miner’s lettuce\, chickweed\, stinging nettle\, wild radish\,
  and more.\n\nWe’ll also explore the unique ecology of the redwood ripar
 ian zone\, getting to know native perennials such as wild ginger\, redwood
  violet\, ferns\, and sheep sorrel. Along the way\, you’ll learn how to 
 prepare simple\, nourishing teas and decoctions using plants like Douglas 
 fir tips\, madrone bark\, dandelion root\, and yerba buena.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Masterclass  Chardonnay\, Pinot Noir\, and Chef-Driven Pairing
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T160000
UID:260420V7OHoQwEXki0oSjOP6vvUQ
DESCRIPTION:Guests are invited to a classroom-style tasting that’s equal
  parts educational and indulgent.\n\nThe experience features our newest re
 leases\, beginning with Chardonnay in all its expressions — from bright 
 and unoaked to spice-driven reserve selections — showcasing how winemaki
 ng choices shape texture and flavor. The lesson continues with three disti
 nct Pinot Noir clones\, moving from light and vivid to rich\, dense\, and 
 deeply layered\, revealing the nuance within a single variety.\n\nEach pou
 r is paired with playful\, crave-worthy bites from Top Chef Dakota Weiss.\
 n\nWhen class ends\, recess begins on the terrace with a final dessert pai
 ring — because every great lesson deserves a sweet reward.
LOCATION:Bouchaine Vineyards
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-masterclass-chardon
 nay-pinot-noir-and-chef-driven-pairings/18628228/2026-04-26T13
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exploring Botanical Monotypes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T170000
UID:260419XdepNZ8HzkWc_hoXbMGhDA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, April 26\, 2026 11:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nE
 xperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nEvent Category: Printmaking\n\nAge\\(s\\)\
 n\n18 and older\n\n$140 – Registration Cost $25 – Materials Fee $165 
 – Total Registration Cost\n\nCreate stunning botanical monotype prints w
 ith spring foliage in this inspiring workshop—perfect for beginners and 
 plant lovers alike!\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nLearn to make stunning\, one-of
 -a-kind botanical prints inspired from the natural world! Join Kelly in th
 is one-day experimental monotype printmaking workshop where you will explo
 re techniques on the printing press. Students will learn how to achieve un
 ique color compositions using local flora as stencils through simple layer
 ing and masking in a supportive group learning environment. Guests are inv
 ited to print using a wide variety of spring foliage and preserved botanic
 als. Kelly will also discuss and demonstrate how to add dimension to print
 s by using textures\, mixed media and collage. It is sure to be a fun and 
 awe-inspiring class for beginners or even experienced printmakers interest
 ed in learning a beautiful new technique. If you love plants\, and you’v
 e always wanted to try monotype\, this class is sure to motivate and inspi
 re you!\n\nMembership has its benefits\n\nAll Silver Memberships and above
  receive 10% off the registration cost for any class purchase over $40. Ma
 terials fees are not discounted.\n\nBecome a member today and find communi
 ty\, connection\, and creativity.\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/exploring-botanical-monotyp
 es/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Calder Quartet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T000000
UID:260416gEfj5ocKM0KamJH6Vxdf-g
DESCRIPTION:The Calder captivates its audience\, exploring a broad spectru
 m of repertoire. Whether performing Beethoven or Bartok\, or commissioning
  a new work\, the Calder strives to fulfill the composer's vision. They po
 ssess a musical curiosity that has brought them the highest of accolades. 
 Their imaginative program includes the music of Barber\, Glass\, Norman\, 
 Price\, and Johnston. Each piece unique and spellbinding.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Junior College
