BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sugarloaf New Volunteer Orientation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T150000
UID:260412y7JTD_YhKUS6w9Hfil63Tw
DESCRIPTION:When you join Sugarloaf's 200\\+ member volunteer commu
 nity\, you gain access to a whole new appreciation for your loc
 al State Park. Make meaningful connections with fellow volunteers\
 , learn new skills\, enjoy time outdoors in a beautiful setting\
 , and play an integral role in keeping Sugarloaf Ridge State Pa
 rk open and accessible for everyone.\n\n Join us at our next vo
 lunteer orientation Sunday April 26\, 2026 from 1:00- 3:00 pm to
  learn what it takes to steward a state park! We'll cover the
  history of Sugarloaf\, how Sonoma Ecology Center operates the p
 ark\, and the various volunteer opportunities available. Beyond th
 e mandatory initial orientation\, trainings and docent enrichment 
 activities will take place periodically\, depending on your intere
 sts and role. \n\nHere are some of the vital ways that voluntee
 rs support Sugarloaf's operations:\n\nServe as docents at the Visi
 tor Center\n\nDirect visitors at the entrance kiosk\n\nAssist with
  data collection and entry\, like our extensive Critter Cam wild
 life tracking project\n\nAid project research and grant-writing\n\nW
 ork on trail and park maintenance projects\n\nFacilitate special e
 vents and parking\n\nSpanish/English literacy and conversational flu
 ency is a plus
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/sugarloaf-new-volunteer
 -orientation/18524116/2026-04-26T13
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Passport to Dry Creek Valley 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T160000
UID:260412w2m9pX6CJkOdmsjm9SZMNg
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us and 25\\+ wineries per day for Pass
 port to Dry Creek Valley\, California’s Friendliest Wine \\+ Food Festi
 val! Travel throughout 16 X 2 idyllic miles and enjoy sun-soaked viney
 ards\, laughter amongst friends\, and unforgettable experiences in wo
 rld-class wine\, food\, and musical entertainment!\n\nSingle-day passes
  available for a taste of the magic as well as weekend passes to s
 oak it all in! Meet founders & winemakers\, taste award-winning win
 es and hyper-local foodie bites\, and enjoy live music and DJ beats! P
 lus\, full access to insider perks all weekend long.\n\nThe perfect blend 
 of tradition and innovation\, Dry Creek Valley is where serious wine is cr
 afted in a delightfully relaxed environment. It honors the legendary famil
 ies who have been here for generations\, and is as much about the communit
 y as it is about the land and the wine.\n\nYou’re supporting the legacy 
 of Dry Creek Valley's agriculture\, story and our non-profit organization 
 – celebrating the valley\, its wineries\, farmers\, grape growers and co
 mmunity!\n\nExperience soil to sip – taste the land. Looks good in the g
 lass. Even better when you taste it.\n\nWhether it’s your first year or 
 one of many\, there is an immense amount to discover — and rediscover!
LOCATION:Dry Creek Valley AVA
URL:https://www.drycreekvalley.org/dcv-passport/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edible & Medicinal Plant Walk Sonoma (Jenner)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T153000
UID:260412dvg5QoEsoEaKqxEI3Pv03w
DESCRIPTION:Join botanist Autumn Summers near beautiful Jenner to learn ab
 out edible and medicinal spring plants of the Sonoma Coast.\n\nWhat if the
  land around you wasn’t just scenery\, but a living apothecary and pantr
 y\, rich with nourishment and healing? When we learn about the medicinal a
 nd edible gifts of our native plants\, we deepen our connection to place\,
  to tradition\, to ourselves\, and to our communities. This knowledge lets
  a sense of belonging bloom inside of us\, inspiring stewardship and weavi
 ng us into the wild and living story of our precious natural homes.\n\nJoi
 n herbalist\, botanist\, and educator Autumn Summers for a guided walk thr
 ough the Bay Area’s edible spring plant landscape. Along the way\, you'l
 l meet native medicinal allies like yarrow\, bay laurel\, stinging nettle\
 , and more\, experiencing their properties firsthand and learning how to 
 identify\, sustainably harvest\, and work with them for food and medicine.
  This walk is an invitation to slow down\, observe\, learn\, and reconnect
 —so you can step away with the skills and confidence to explore the worl
 d of wild herbalism foraging on your own.
LOCATION:Sonoma Coast
URL:https://www.forkinthepath.org/schedule/plant-class-sonoma-2026-a629h
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
