DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T153000
UID:260324rP8kFl0VCEG7mhyFAdCLqQ
DESCRIPTION:Cinnabar Theater presents The Christians by Lucas Hnath\n\nA p
 owerful\, thought-provoking drama about faith\, conviction\, and the cost 
 of standing by your beliefs.\n\nWhen a beloved megachurch pastor delivers 
 a sermon that challenges a core doctrine\, his congregation is thrown into
  turmoil. What follows is an intimate and gripping exploration of belief\,
  doubt\, leadership\, and community—inviting audiences to wrestle with b
 ig questions that linger long after the final moment on stage.\n\n• Warr
 en Theater\, Sonoma State University (Ives Hall)\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, 
 Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\n• April 10–26\, 2026\n\n• Fridays & Satur
 days at 7:30 PM | Sundays at 2:00 PM\n\n• Special Talkback Post Show: Su
 nday\, April 19\n\nDirected by Nathan Cummings and featuring a stellar cas
 t\, this minimalist\, emotionally resonant production is recommended for m
 ature audiences.\n\nTickets: cinnabartheater.org
LOCATION:Warren Theater\, Sonoma State University (Ives Hall)\,
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thechristians/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to Mid Range Soda Firing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T180000
UID:260324pq9lB9C40UqxwjGtEThDgQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, April 25: 9 AM – 5 PM\; Sunday\, Apri
 l 26: 10 Am – 6 PM \;Tuesday\, April 28: 4 PM – 7 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRo
 om 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nEvent Cate
 gories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n17\\+\n\n$295 – Registrati
 on Cost\n\nAbout the Class\n\nThis workshop is an introduction to mid-rang
 e soda firing\, with hands-on training in the process of loading\, firing\
 , and maintaining our crossdraft kiln named “Julia”. Participants in t
 his workshop will learn the fundamentals of atmospheric soda firing. The c
 lass will be instructed in the safety and care of the equipment as well as
  guided through the firing process. This workshop includes instruction on 
 glazing\, wadding the ceramic pieces\, loading the kiln\, firing the kiln\
 , and kiln maintenance. Demos and Lectures will also happen during the fir
 ing. Participants will bring bisque-ware to be fired as bare clay or with 
 slipped surfaces. There will be an assortment of flashing slips and glazes
  to apply to the bisqueware on loading day for those who choose to use the
 m.  Each participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. \\(Tip\; Make sur
 e all your pots fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot 
 of space\\). This firing will be a reduction fired cone 6 with sprayed sod
 a at the end.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/intro-to-mid-range-soda-fir
 ing-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
