BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI\, Scams and Elder Abuse Awareness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T140000
UID:260407rGfiUFNcOEi0Ey_jnbE8gA
DESCRIPTION:The speakers for this talk will be Dan Ryan with Redwood Credi
 t Union\, an AI expert\, Crista Barnett with Senior Advocacy Services Nort
 h Bay\, and Amanda Esposti\, the Windsor Police Dept Community Services Of
 ficer. Using examples\, they will give you tips on how to recognize AI gen
 erated material\, scams\, and elder abuse\, plus provide tips on what to d
 o to protect yourself. Amanda will wrap up the talk to let you know what W
 indsor Police Dept has seen lately in our area. A car safety hammer is inc
 luded\, while supplies last\, one per family. The talk is free for all to 
 attend\, so please share this invite.\n\nTo register go to https://bit.ly/
 ScamsAISeminar or call the Senior Center at 707-838-1260. Pre-registration
  is not required but is recommended for the Car Safety Hammer giveaway. Fo
 r those of you who don’t drive\, there will be an alternative giveaway. 
 This presentation is part of the Windsor Ready Talk series hosted by the T
 own of Windsor and Windsor COPE. For more information email windsor\\_cope
 @yahoo.com.
LOCATION:Windsor Recreation Senior Center
URL:https://bit.ly/ScamsAISeminar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:April Poetry Salon & Book Festival Presented by Timothy Williams
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T190000
UID:2604048TgDjys_LUuqyr04XYkXog
DESCRIPTION:**April Poetry Salon: Book Festival – National Poetry Month 
 in Downtown Santa Rosa**\n\nCelebrate **National Poetry Month** with a spe
 cial **Poetry Salon: Book Festival** at **Barrel Proof Lounge in Downtown 
 Santa Rosa**.\n\nThis unique evening blends **live poetry\, prose\, music\
 , and book readings** into an intimate\, creative space built for connecti
 on and expression.\n\nFeaturing local voices including: **Claire Drucker\,
  Shawna\, Brian\, Swetech\, and Martens**\, plus a welcoming **open mic** 
 for writers ready to share their work.\n\nHave a book? Bring it. Read from
  it. Share your voice.\n\nThis is a **“listening room” experience** 
 — a supportive\, attentive audience where words take center stage.\n\n**
 Event Details:** 📅 Tuesday\, April 28\, 2026 🕔 5–7 PM 📍 Barrel 
 Proof Lounge — 501 Mendocino Ave\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nPerfect for fa
 ns of **poetry readings\, spoken word\, book launches\, and literary event
 s in Sonoma County**.\n\nCome read\, listen\, and celebrate the written wo
 rd.\n\n21+\n\nCheck out BarrelProofLounge.com for more events in Downtown 
 Santa Rosa.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/april-poetry-salon-book-festival-presente
 d-by-timothy-williams-tickets-1986700160661?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
