END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T180000
UID:260415zA-xTekAbEyqkMdvrdAPNw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Reptile Expo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T150000
UID:260415v5QSTeDzDEytcXQotEkl8Q
DESCRIPTION:Santa Rosa Reptile Expo - May 2–3\, 2026 - Sonoma County Eve
 nt Center at the Fairgrounds – Santa Rosa\, CA Explore a huge selection 
 of incredible animals including tarantulas\, amphibians\, snakes\, chamele
 ons\, geckos\, monitors\, bearded dragons\, jumping spiders\, tortoises\, 
 turtles\, and much more. Whether you're a seasoned keeper\, a collector\, 
 or just curious about the reptile world\, there is something for everyone.
  Browse vendor booths offering a wide variety of bioactive supplies\, feed
 ers\, plants\, tanks and enclosures\, cork bark\, grapevine\, dry goods\, 
 and reptile care products. Take advantage of exclusive expo-only deals whi
 le finding everything you need to create the perfect habitat for your anim
 als. The expo will also feature live animal shows\, including appearances 
 by amazing animals such as the Patagonian cavy mara and North American opo
 ssum\, alligator & more! Guests can also enjoy a hands-on terrarium buildi
 ng workshop. Watch and learn how to build a bioactive enclosure\, or upgra
 de your experience and build your own terrarium to take home — perfect f
 or your new pet. Bring the whole family and experience one of Northern Cal
 ifornia’s most exciting reptile and exotic animal events. Sonoma County 
 Event Center at the Fairgrounds 1350 Bennett Valley Road\, Santa Rosa\, CA
  95404 Sat. 10AM-5PM Sun. 10AM-4PM Two-day passes and Family discounts pac
 ks also available online. Get tickets\, directions\, more info at https://
 www.CVRExpo.com
LOCATION:Sonoma County Fair & Event Center
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2340860243091693/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature as Medicine: Forest Immersion Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T170000
UID:260415o1r5M1HBZEid8u4yQ88kRQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a stress-relieving Nature as Medicine session on t
 he SSU Fairfield Osborn Preserve. The session will be led by Sarah Murphy\
 , MD\, a Family and Integrative Medicine physician who works at the SSU St
 udent Health Center. \n\nThis will be a mellow\, calm\, tech-free immersi
 on in nature where you will pay close attention to sensory details around 
 you to develop a sense of presence and connection. \n\nStudies on forest 
 immersion experiences like this have demonstrated they decrease stress lev
 els\, anxiety\, and low mood\, and increase attention\, feelings of connec
 tedness and well-being\, and even help boost the immune system. We hope th
 e experience will help you feel refreshed\, grounded\, and mentally rechar
 ged.
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/nature_as_medicine_osborn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
