BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:260218_9YTBDBgQkKfeXW1nSb2kg
DESCRIPTION:Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter Concert Sunday\, May 3\, 2026 
  3 -5pm\n\nSt. Columba’s Inverness Music Series presents Lisa Lynne & Ar
 yeh Frankfurter: Celtic Harps\, Rare Instruments & Wondrous Stories. \n\n
 Step into an afternoon of enchantment with Lisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter\
 , an internationally acclaimed duo whose music is as expansive as it is in
 timate. Drawing from Celtic\, Nordic\, and Eastern European traditions\, t
 hey weave breathtaking soundscapes on Celtic harps\, Swedish nyckelharpa\,
  Ukrainian bandura\, bouzouki\, cittern\, and other rare instruments. With
  roots in street performing and rock music\, and a combined million-plus a
 lbums sold\, their concerts blend virtuosic musicianship\, original and tr
 aditional melodies\, humor\, and storytelling—inviting audiences into a 
 spellbinding journey of beauty\, wonder\, and joy. \n\nAdvance tickets $2
 5\, $30 at door\n\nLisa Lynne & Aryeh Frankfurter are a multi-instrumental
 ist duo with Celtic Harps\, Swedish Nyckelharpa\, Ukrainian Bandura\, Bouz
 ouki\, Cittern and more. They hail from Oregon and tour extensively\, both
  having successful recording and performing careers built from years of st
 reet performing and a background as rock musicians. They have performed wi
 th some of the biggest names in folk and acoustic music and have sold well
  over a million albums combined. Audiences are spellbound and enchanted wi
 th their unique show of breathtaking music both Traditional and original\,
  with wondrous stories and humor entwined.\n\nGet your tickets at https://
 www.stcolumbasinverness.org/music-series-lisa-aryeh
LOCATION:St. Columba's Inverness
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/lisa-lynne-aryeh-frankf
 urter-concert/18143894/2026-05-03T15
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TJ KLUNE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T153000
UID:260104Yt7SDfrPskmFwo0IYCVeaw
DESCRIPTION:SEBASTOPOL --\n\nCopperfield’s Books is delighted to welcome
  perennial staff favorite and *New York Times* bestselling author TJ Klun
 e to Sebastopol in celebration of his enchanting and deeply stirring new n
 ovel — *We Burned So Bright.*\n\nThis is a ticketed\, off-site event at
  The Sebastopol Community Cultural Center.\n\nEach ticket (book+tax) inclu
 des admission for one\, seating and a signed hardcover of *We Burned So B
 right.*\n\nJoin us for a reading and warm discussion followed by an audien
 ce Q&A and book-signing with photo opportunities!\n\nScholarships availabl
 e - Dying to attend but can't afford the ticket? Tell us why you can’t m
 iss this special afternoon by emailing jmadsen@copperbook.com\n\n**A heart
 -wrenching standalone novel by #1 *New York Times* bestselling author TJ
  Klune\,*We Burned So Bright* follows an elder gay couple on an end-of-th
 e-world road-trip.**\n\n*The road stretched out before them. No other cars
 \, just the headlights on the blacktop. Above\, the cracked moon in a kale
 idoscope sky….*\n\nHusbands Don and Rodney have lived a good long life. 
 Together they’ve experienced the highest highs of love and family\, and 
 lows so low that they felt like the end of the world.\n\nNow\, the world i
 s ending for real. A rogue black hole is coming for Earth and in a month e
 verything and everyone they’ve ever known will be gone.\n\nSuddenly\, af
 ter 40 years together\, Don and Rodney are out of time. They’re in a rac
 e against the clock to make it from Maine to Washington State to take care
  of some unfinished business before it’s all over.\n\nOn the road they m
 eet those who refuse to believe death is coming and those who rush to meet
  it. But there are also people living their final days as best they know h
 ow—impromptu weddings\, bright burning bonfires\, shared meals\, and new
  friends.\n\nAnd as the black hole draws near\, among ball lightning and u
 nder a cracked moon in a kaleidoscope sky\, Don and Rodney will look back 
 on their lives and ask if their best was good enough.\n\nIs it enough to b
 urn bright if nothing comes from the ashes?\n\n**Author: TJ KLUNE** (he/
 him) is the *New York Times* and *USA Today* bestselling\, Lambda Lite
 rary Award-winning author of *The House in the Cerulean Sea*\, *Under th
 e Whispering Door*\, *In the Lives of Puppets*\, the Green Creek Series f
 or adults\, the Extraordinaries Series for teens\, and more. Being queer h
 imself\, Klune believes it's important—now more than ever—to have accu
 rate\, positive queer representation in stories.\n\n**PRAISE FOR...**\n\n*
 *For *Somewhere Beyond the Sea:*** **A #1 New York Times\, #1 USA Today a
 nd #1 indie bestseller!** "An enchanting sequel about found family." — 
 ***The New York Times*** **For *In the Lives of Puppets:*** **A *New Yor
 k Times*\, *Sunday Times* and indie bestseller!**\n\n"Thoroughly enterta
 ining and deeply stirring." — **Chuck Tingle\, Hugo Award finalist and 
 author of *Camp Damascus*** **For U*nder the Whispering Door:*** **A *Ne
 w York Times*\, *USA Today* and indie bestseller!**\n\n“Tenderness\, w
 it\, and skillful worldbuilding elevate this delightful tale. Fans of quee
 r fantasy won’t want to miss this.” **— *Publishers Weekly*** **For
  *The House in the Cerulean Sea:*** **A *New York Times*\, *USA Today*\
 , and indie bestseller!**\n\n"I loved it. It is like being wrapped up in a
  big gay blanket. Simply perfect." **— V.E. Schwab\, #1 *New York Time
 s* bestselling author of *The Invisible Life of Addie LaRue*** **For *Th
 e Bones Beneath My Skin:*** **A *New York Times*\, *USA Today*\, and ind
 ie bestseller!**\n\n"An uplifting and curious novel\, a shining dot on an 
 overlapping Venn diagram of sci-fi\, fantasy\, adventure and gay romance."
  **— *Aurealis***
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://TJKLUNE_SEBASTOPOL.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Symphony - Shakespeare in Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:25121780HFIsa2lkeBHFphhJ3BHQ
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare in Music\n\nMay 2\, 3 & 4\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Claire Hua
 ngci\,** piano\n\n**Nicola Vann\,** actor\n\n**SAMUEL COLERIDGE-TAYLOR:** 
 Incidental Music from *Othello*\n\n**WOLFGANG AMADEUS MOZART:** Concerto N
 o. 20 in D minor for Piano and Orchestra\, K. 466\n\n**PYOTR ILYICH TCHAIK
 OVSKY:** *Hamlet* (Fantasy Overture) in F minor\, Opus 67\n\n**PYOTR ILYIC
 H TCHAIKOVSKY:** *Romeo and Juliet* (Fantasy Overture) in B minor\n\nStep 
 into the world of Shakespeare’s dramatic\, enduring tales. Tchaikovsky
 ’s passionate *Romeo and Juliet* is a timeless and familiar classic\, wh
 ile Coleridge-Taylor’s evocative *Othello* offers a compelling counterpo
 int for interpreting Shakespeare in music. Plus\, pianist Claire Huangci m
 akes her Weill Hall debut with Mozart’s expressive Piano Concerto No. 20
 .\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\, and prices are subject to change without
  notice. Tickets are subject to availability.\n\nPhoto by  Jean-Baptiste 
 Millot
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
