BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Handbuilding 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T123000
UID:260325plgiS22D-kOkAJZt_Iykqw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nMondays\, March 30 – May 18\, 2026 9:30 AM – 1
 2:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nA
 ll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Extended Classes\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n
 \n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Re
 gistration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nLearn the fundamentals of creating handbuilt\,
  functional objects with clay in this 8 week course. Thoughtfully explore 
 the tried and true techniques of ceramic work!\n\nAbout the Class\n\nDebor
 ah Donahower takes you through the fundamentals of working with clay in ha
 nd building in this 8 week course. Designed for all levels \\(beginners an
 d those more experienced\\) Deborah thoughtfully explores the tried and tr
 ue techniques of ceramic work with her students through structured assignm
 ents\, allowing her students to develop their own creative voice in the pr
 ocess. This course will emphasize building functional forms with creative 
 surface design in mind\; focusing on forms with large areas to explore tex
 ture\, painterly surface techniques\, and much more. Students will receive
  instruction in hand building\, and basic glazing techniques.  With your 
 8 week class registration\, students receive the opportunity to purchase a
  studio pass for ½ off during the duration of their class. Sign ups for m
 embership will be included in your pre class email
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/handbuilding-101/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Small Wonders
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T170000
UID:260324HJ3Jt6XNm06WwZgNPZC6Nw
DESCRIPTION:Call for Art: Small Wonders\n\nSome of the most exquisite beau
 ty can be captured in the smallest of images and objects: the iridescence 
 of a hummingbird in flight\, a millefiori paperweight\, Faberge eggs\, or 
 a miniature woven basket. These pieces are modest in size but powerful in 
 creativity and expression.\n\nHealdsburg Center for the Arts \\(HCA\\) inv
 ites artists to submit paintings\, original fine art prints\, collage\, mi
 xed media\, drawings\, fiber arts\, sculptures\, ceramics\, and jewelry fo
 r this exhibition.\n\nApplication Requirements:\n\n- Platform: All applica
 tions must be submitted via EntryThingy\n\n- Eligibility: Work must be ori
 ginal and completed within the past two years. Photos in the application m
 ust represent the actual work intended for exhibition.\n\n- Size/Weight: A
 rtwork must not exceed 12" x 12" unframed \\(144 sq in\\) or 196 sq in fra
 med. Maximum weight is 40 lbs.\n\n- Display: 2-D pieces must be securely w
 ired \\(no alligator clips\\). 3-D work must be stable\; artists are respo
 nsible for on-site assembly if required.\n\n- Sales: All work must be for 
 sale. HCA retains a 40% commission\; artists receive 60%. Please list reta
 il prices only.\n\nKey Dates:\n\n- Entry Deadline: May 10\, 2026 \\(9 PM\\
 )\n\n- Notification of Selection: By May 13\, 2026\n\n- Shipped Work Deadl
 ine: Wednesday\, May 27\, 2026 \\(must include pre-paid return label\\)\n\
 n- Hand-Delivery: Sunday\, May 31 \\(12–4 PM\\) and Monday\, June 1 \\(1
 1 AM–1 PM\\)\n\n- Exhibition Dates: June 4\, 2026 – July 19\, 2026\n\n
