BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Art Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T170000
UID:2604010CU6NS3slkiUMRqC--ibsA
DESCRIPTION:4 - 18\\+ yrs Adult participation optional Class Experience To
 gether\, we will breathe and enjoy the feel of our hands creating with col
 orful textural materials. This class is designed for littles ones and thei
 r families to unwind and decompress in the late afternoon and enjoy proces
 s art. We will create with a variety of materials that will be set out in 
 an open ended\, Reggio Emelia style where students are offered invitations
  to play with the materials. We will explore different themes such as pain
 ting with acrylic or tempera\; do collages with various types of paper and
  mixed media\; practice sculpture\; or just make creative art with recycle
 d materials. The only assignment is to play and explore with colors\, shap
 es\, and textures\, with no messy clean-up at home! "Play is a key compone
 nt of the arts and aesthetics in myriad ways. Art and play are like two si
 des of the same coin\, with play being a part of artistic expression\, ima
 gination\, creativity\, and curiosity." - Susan Magsamen\,  Your Brain on 
 Art: How the Arts Transform Us Amanda Rose Hopkins has a Bachelor of Fine 
 Arts from UC Santa Cruz and thereafter she worked as an apprentice artist 
 at the Sarnath International Nyingma Institute\, near Varanasi\, India. Sh
 e has been working with children since 2009. She completed a multiple subj
 ect teaching credential program and has worked locally at Sunridge Charter
  School\, The REACH School\, Sebastopol Center for the Arts and Santa Rosa
  Junior College. She has studied multicultural education\, Positive Discip
 line\, Toolbox and child development. Notes Land of the Good Members get 2
 0% \\(!\\) off this class using code: 2026member To utilize the discount\,
  please first activate a membership or email us at hello@landofthegood.com
  if you need help subscribing! Class Requirements Students need to be full
 y potty-trained and able to communicate/navigate self-care needs. What you
 'll learn Students will be exposed to methods of painting Various types of
  paintbrushes Acrylic painting Tempera painting Oil pastel drawing Collage
  Types of adhesives and their uses Sculptural techniques Recycled art Samp
 le Class Format 3:15pm - 5:00pm\; late drop-off or early pick-up are fine 
 as this is an open-art lab and children may have varying capacity. Parents
  or other supervising adults are welcome to stay and participate or enjoy 
 tea & coffee and use the high-speed internet/cowork during class time. Ple
 ase pick up promptly by 5pm. Other Things To Know Adult Participation Opti
 onal. One adult View more
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Junior College
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/family-art-lab/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BFA Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T160000
UID:260417sKaRE3R5GEmyWTeU8bpOtQ
DESCRIPTION:Each spring\, the University Art Gallery proudly presents the 
 Bachelor of Fine Arts \\(BFA\\) Exhibition\, showcasing the work of Sonoma
  State University's graduating BFA class. The 2026 BFA Exhibition will be 
 on view April 23-May 23\, 2026. Offered by SSU's Art Department\, the BFA 
 degree is distinguished from the BA by its rigorous\, studio-intensive cur
 riculum. The program requires an additional year of focused study\, includ
 ing advanced coursework in studio art\, art history\, and art theory. Ofte
 n regarded as the degree of choice for students pursuing graduate or profe
 ssional studies\, the BFA fosters significant artistic development within 
 a concentrated creative environment. For both students and faculty\, this 
 exhibition represents a culminating achievement-an opportunity to present 
 a carefully curated selection of each artist's strongest work in a profess
 ional gallery setting\, exhibited alongside their peers. Opening Reception
 : Thursday\, April 23\, 2026 4:00-6:00 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/bfa-exhibition/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Morning Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T094000
UID:260412XUNRMQ71IU-ln0fX4ouz6A
DESCRIPTION:Regenerative Ayurvedic Yoga with Tirza Dawn Come\, step onto y
 our mat with an open heart and an open mind. Invest in your self care and 
 join us for morning yoga in the OCA studio. $20 per class\, $15 for OCA me
 mbers. Each Wednesday from 9:00-10:15 AM in our Studio. Pay at the door fo
 r a-la-carte sessions or use the links below to pay ahead for four weeks a
 t a time.  Pay Online 4 sessions - OCA members  Pay Online 4 sessions - no
 n members Tirza Dawn Naramore is a yogi\, mother\, artist\, ceremonialist 
 and lover of life. She has been practicing and teaching yoga and meditatio
 n for 30 years and offers yoga retreats and trainings that center on optim
 um health\, self realization and self love. Her teachers are from many yog
 a and tantric traditions\, but her primary lineages are Iyengar and Kali R
 ay.  Tirza is deeply devoted to community building and is honored to have 
 created a number of community supported non profits including Mystic Famil
 y Circus and The AWAKEN Project\, which serves families with children on t
 he autism spectrum. Tirza is proud to be the mother of 3 wild teenagers\, 
 including her incredible son who is diagnosed with autism. Tirza's spiritu
 ality is one of many influences and teachings. Beginning with a Christian 
 up-bringing and being raised on a Christian commune in her early childhood
 \, she later expanded into more earth-based ways. While in her 20's Tirza 
 was adopted into the Native American Church\, where she learned from her r
 elatives a way of living the "Beauty Way." During the 1990's and early 200
 0's\, Tirza lived in San Francisco\, Oakland and Berkeley\, directing the 
 Mystic Family Circus\, which was a performance group dedicated to cultural
  awareness and bridge building. She worked with Cirque du Soleil\, Burning
  Man\, Reclaiming\, Contraband\, CELLspace and other Bay Area art collecti
 ves and non profits to provide conscious entertainment and "prayerformance
 s" for the betterment of humankind and the planet. In 2012\, Tirza helped 
 to found the Buckeye Gathering\, an ancestral skills gathering in Northern
  California which draws teachers and students of all ages to learn ancestr
 al ways of tending the earth and survival skills. Tirza Dawn was the found
 er of yoga programming and the Ayurvedic Yoga Teacher Trainings at the dhy
 ana Center of Ayurveda in Sebastopol\, California\, which operated a commu
 nity center of healing and education from 2010 to 2020.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/ew6dc3w3s87
 emgn-f7ghs-2rk62-3zdlw-4mf4n-ymprd-c99rn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
