SUMMARY:Makers Market™ Local Artist Fair @ First Street Napa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T170000
UID:260219ifHsiVIliUiempaV1YKf-w
DESCRIPTION:Join Makers Market™ to kick off the 2026 Local Artist Fairs 
 at First Street Napa! Get ready for another season of creativity\, communi
 ty\, and incredible goods made here in the Bay Area. Come support talented
  makers\, discover beautiful artisan products\, and enjoy a fun-filled day
  outdoors!\n\nWHEN? Saturday\, May 9 | 11am - 5pm\n\nWHERE? First Street N
 apa in Napa\, CA\n\n- 40\\+ local makers\n\n- Handmade jewelry\, pottery\,
  fragrances\, candles\, bath and body\, apparel\, leather goods\, and more
 !\n\n- Kid- and pet-friendly\n\n- Enjoy live music by local musicians\n\n-
  Stop into the Makers Market™ brick-and-mortar store \\(in Suite 301\, a
 djacent to the fair\\) and shop even more unique\, American-made products.
 \n\nShare with your shopping buddies and mark your calendars! Can't wait t
 o see you there!\n\n- - -\n\nAre you a maker looking to sell your products
  at the Local Artist Street Fair? Register here:\n\nhttps://makersmarket.u
 s/maker-registration/\n\n- - -\n\nMakers Market is locally founded and ind
 ependently owned\, with brick-and-mortar stores in Alpharetta\, Napa\, San
 tana Row\, Lafayette\, and Mill Valley. We aim to bring you products that 
 honor the ideals of American craftsmanship and are modern\, handmade\, and
  sustainably produced. Join us in our mission of Rebuilding the Legacy of 
 American Made\, while supporting our local artists\, local economies\, and
  the community. Come visit one of our stores today!\n\nhttps://makersmarke
 t.us/locations/
LOCATION:First Street Napa
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1770863670938322/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T101500
UID:260212tlbhSehNaEW8o67fMoAM7w
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on first
 \, second and fourth Saturdays of the month from 9:45 - 10:15 AM at ​Uni
 tarian Universalist Congregation of Marin\, 240 Channing Way\, San Rafael 
 CA 94903. Contact: Sue M. 415-298-6792​. You may view all North Bay OA 
 in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html\
 n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recover
 y by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles
 —one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program
 .\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any sp
 ecific food plan. \n\nIf food is causing problems in your life\, you don
 ’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and help is available.
 \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https://www.nort
 hbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. The Musers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T180000
UID:26020683Go84NYnkyZ6YSCRpdPag
DESCRIPTION:*Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come 
 together.*\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a ta
 sting room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acr
 oss the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll 
 and Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new so
 unds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\n**The Musers** Rooted in rich 
 musical traditions and diverse acoustic styles\, The Musers blend powerf
 ul vocals\, intricate guitar work\, and lively rhythms into a genre-crossi
 ng\, high-spirited sound. \n\n**Details**\n\nNo cover. Walk-ins are welco
 me\, but this event tends to fill up quickly\, so we recommend making a re
 servation. We are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River History Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T120000
UID:260129fa-NbQRKQEuu0MagSPg29g
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a uniquely Petaluma experience on the water. This two-ho
 ur\, gentle guided kayak tour launches from The Floathouse Petaluma and ex
 plores the river that once served as the region's "saltwater highway." Lon
 g before roads and railways\, the Petaluma River powered San Francisco\, t
 he Gold Rush miners\, and even global markets with the produce from local 
 farms and industries\, supplying everything from eggs to overalls.\n\nDesi
 gned and led by a Petaluman\, actor and former history teacher this entert
 aining and enlightening tour brings history to life through storytelling e
 nhanced by costumed actors on shore. You'll hear fascinating stories from 
 the perspectives of long-ago Petalumans—young workers\, entrepreneurs\, 
 and colorful characters whose daily lives revolved around the river.\n\nPa
 ddle in stable sit-on-top kayaks through and beyond Petaluma's charming do
 wntown\, while gaining a deeper appreciation for how this tidal waterway s
 haped the city and the region. Visitors are often surprised by how much th
 ey learn—and many come back with friends.\n\n$75 per person\, all-inclus
 ive. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/petaluma-river-history-
 paddle/17975629/2026-05-09T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
