BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T180000
UID:260415ZpCFj4bhYEuAuDZQBG8Tdg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seussical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T160000
UID:260414cOmzvM9OH06BHamkS9lrTA
DESCRIPTION:Join the Cat in the Hat\, Horton the Elephant\, and all your f
 avorite Dr. Seuss characters in Seussical\, the high-energy\, heartwarming
  musical that brings these beloved stories to life! With toe-tapping songs
 \, dazzling visuals\, and a story about friendship\, bravery\, and believi
 ng in the impossible\, this family-friendly extravaganza is pure joy from 
 start to finish.\n\n***Seussical***\n\nMay 1 - 17\, 2026\n\nFriday at 7:30
 pm\, Saturday & Sunday matinee at 2:00pm\n\n\\* Saturday\, May 2nd at 2:00
 pm is a Pick-Your-Price Performance\, tickets are available on a sliding s
 cale starting at $10\n\nMusic by Stephen Flaherty\n\nLyrics by Lynn Ahrens
 \n\nBased on the Works of Theodor Geisel (Dr. Seuss)\n\nDirected by Kim Br
 omley\n\nMusic Direction by Lucas Sherman\n\nChoreography by Karen Miles\n
 \nFeaturing: Nelson Brown\, Monica Burrowes\, AJ Correia\, Sara Curtis\, A
 lex Delzell\, Katie Foster\, Mallory Gold\, Riz Gross\, Michael Hunter\, R
 on Lam\, Molly Larsen-Shine\, Addie Lowe\, Olivia Manz\, Michelle Pagano\,
  Orion Pudoff\, Peter Rogers\, Ted Smith\, Nicole Stanley\, Tina Traboulsi
 \, Malik Charles D. Wade I and Aliya Webb
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=290251
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Postcards - Spring 2026 Concert Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T170000
UID:260412vXdbw_gzAkyw8UMl-HJBeQ
DESCRIPTION:The Occidental Community Choir puts on live concerts featuring
  an eclectic mix of locally composed music\, classical and contemporary ch
 oral pieces\, poetry\, and spoken word from our community in the redwoods 
 of Northern California.\n\nThe Occidental Community Choir invites audience
 s to its Spring concert series\, Postcards\, a musical journey through mem
 ory\, connection\, and the moments that shape our lives.In times that can 
 feel uncertain or isolating\, even small gestures of connection—a postca
 rd\, a call\, a simple message saying “I’m thinking of you”—can re
 mind us that we are not alone. Postcards is built around that spirit of re
 aching out. Each piece in the program serves as a musical postcard: a snap
 shot from a particular time and place\, carrying stories of joy\, longing\
 , hope\, and reflection.\n\nSome of these musical postcards arrive bright 
 and sun-drenched\; others carry the weathered edges of memory. Together th
 ey form a collection of moments that remind us our lives are measured not 
 only in years\, but in the experiences that stay with us and the ones we s
 hare with others.Through song\, the choir becomes both sender and recipien
 t—offering voices as messages of care\, presence\, and connection. Postc
 ards is a reminder that even in difficult times\, music can help us reach 
 across distance and say something simple and powerful: you matter\, you ar
 e connected\, and you are not alone.\n\nJoin the Occidental Community Choi
 r this spring for an evening of music that carries stories\, memories\, an
 d hope into a weary and waiting world.
LOCATION:Glaser Center
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/postcards-spring-2026-c
 oncert-series/18501382/2026-05-10T15
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
