BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life & Times of Emily Chabot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T180000
UID:260419Vu5aNjLJeUiM64lD-4qNZA
DESCRIPTION:The St. Helena Public Library will host a free talk on Tuesday
 \, May 12\, 2026\, at 4:00 pm.\, titled "The Life & Times of Emily Chabot.
 " The program will be presented by Karen Mireau\, "Literary Midwife" and f
 ounder of Karen Mireau Books. Emily was a pioneer feminist and philanthrop
 ist and a passionate supporter of women artists and scientists. Among many
  other contributions to California history\, she co-founded a hospital in 
 Oakland that was the forerunner of Kaiser Permanente. Come learn about Emi
 ly's extraordinary life and the history of San Francisco in the 1800s. Kar
 en Mireau is the publisher of Emily Chabot: A Memoir by Lucy Rau Ferguson.
  Books will be available at the program.\n\n***Contact:***\n\n**Mara Stric
 kler**\n\n**St. Helena Public Library**\n\n**1492 Library Lane**\n\n**St. 
 Helena\, CA 94574**\n\n**mstrickler@cityofsthelena.gov**\n\n**707-963-5244
 **
LOCATION:St. Helena Public Library
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-life-times-of-emily
 -chabot/18644635/2026-05-12T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
